For equal distances, sum the travel times before dividing total distance by total time.
\[
\begin{aligned}
\overline{v} &= \frac{3}{\frac{1}{20}+\frac{1}{30}+\frac{1}{60}}\\
&= 30.00\text{ km/h}
\end{aligned}
\]
The alternative \(36.67\text{ km/h}\) is the arithmetic mean of the speeds, rounded to two decimal places; it assumes equal times instead of equal distances.

